  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HgSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>dil</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> with alkyne gives addition of water as per markonikoff&#39;s rule.</p><p><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>HgSO</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></munderover><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math></p><p>Hence, by this process preparation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math><br />Cann&#39;t possible.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6391ae6b-79ce-4cdd-8a41-a0ac1353c588-ascaa.png\" style=\"width: 429px; height: 348px;\" /></p><p>Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CHO</mi></math> cannot be formed.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3278593f-7584-4df0-acef-3c68916d624a-image.png\" style=\"width: 351px; height: 159px;\" /></p>",
